INSERT INTO public.reference_layouts (id, category_id, name, prompt, created_at) VALUES ('ed82c443-c9a8-4fbb-b2b2-f09bbba92661', 'ed408554-3ce0-44c0-8ab1-78b45f8859e7', 'Demo Brand Right-Side Hero', 'BACKGROUND ASSET ONLY.
The application renders every headline, subhead, statistic, bullet, CTA, logo, label, chart value, and navigation mark after this image is generated. Create only the nonverbal visual layer. Do not draw or imitate any letters, numbers, words, logos, watermarks, labels, badges, buttons, charts with values, or text-shaped marks.
The copy reserve must be genuine negative space made by composition, crop, lighting, blur, atmosphere, or one continuous color field. Never draw a text-holder box, blank card, empty panel, placeholder rectangle, banner, framed copy area, fake form, empty table, or callout container in that reserve. Do not outline or shade the reserve as a separate object.
A genuine product screen, dashboard, device, report, or application interface is allowed only when the supplied evidence supports it and only as the primary subject inside the visual zone; it must never be an empty container for later copy. Leave the deterministic overlay zone quiet, continuous, and low-detail.

PURPOSE: Create a right-weighted hero background with a permanently clear left copy zone. Create a square 1:1, 1080x1080 full-bleed AI background for Demo Brand. The result is not a finished poster: deterministic HTML overlays add all real copy, logo, and CTA.

SCENE SELECTION: product or software benefit ÔåÆ use one evidence-backed device, report, dashboard, or UI as the hero subject in the visual zone; people or physical service ÔåÆ use one evidence-backed person, vehicle, workplace, or environmental subject; metric or research finding ÔåÆ use one abstract unlabeled visual motif only when supported; short benefit statement ÔåÆ simplify to one focal reference-supported object; no clear match ÔåÆ preserve this layout''s geometry and reduce visual density rather than inventing a scene.

ADAPTATION BLUEPRINT: Retain one evidence-backed person, product screen, device, vehicle, illustration, or object cluster on the right. Use crop, lighting, blur, or a natural gradient to transition into an open left field; never manufacture a copy container. One primary subject on the right, optional subtle environmental context, and uninterrupted negative space on the left.

LAYOUT: Keep the left 50% as continuous quiet negative space and the right 50% as the visual zone. The primary visual must remain on the right; deterministic text renders on the left. Puppeteer owns the overlay coordinates: text (0, 120), logo (60, 48), CTA (60, 900). The background must not draw a boundary, panel, card, banner, box, or placeholder around those coordinates. Keep every generated object outside the quiet overlay reserve. Preserve observed crop, overlap, whitespace rhythm, and edge alignment. The reserve stays visually continuous with the canvas and has no border, fill patch, card, or panel.

VISUAL EXECUTION: Use saved palette roles #0D80F4, #102F49, and #4A91E8 only where the evidence supports them. Reproduce the observed flat-versus-dimensional balance, corner radii, border weight, shadows, illustration geometry, and foreground/midground/background order.

DENSITY AND LEGIBILITY: One primary subject on the right, optional subtle environmental context, and uninterrupted negative space on the left. Retain one decisive focal point and enough continuous negative space to understand the visual in three seconds. Tiny functional marks may be abstract shapes only; they must not resemble generated marketing text or empty UI.

RESTRICTIONS: 1. Do not replace the uploaded composition with a generic topic symbol or cinematic wallpaper. 2. Do not promote a minor reference icon into the primary hero. 3. Do not put visual modules, texture, glow, or illustrations inside the renderer text-safe zone. 4. Do not invent claims, customer metrics, product capabilities, certifications, or interfaces. 5. Do not change a light reference into a dark neon canvas or a flat reference into photorealism. 6. Do not add people, devices, shields, locks, circuits, dashboards, or charts unless the reference supports them. 7. Do not increase the observed subject, icon, chart, or illustration count merely to fill space. An evidence-backed dashboard may remain one complete hero subject. 8. Do not imitate long source copy; reproduce only the visible design grammar and subject or scene anatomy. 9. Do not render headline, body copy, CTA, logo, watermark, brand name, or decorative fake text. 10. Do not crop the primary visual, break the outer margin, or cover the deterministic overlay reserve. 11. Do not draw a blank card, empty panel, placeholder rectangle, banner, text-holder box, callout box, or framed copy area; negative space must remain part of the continuous background. 12. Every visual-side module must be complete and meaningful: no blank white cards, empty rounded tiles, vacant UI rows, skeleton widgets, unused list panels, or containers waiting for copy. A module is allowed only when its interior is fully occupied by one coherent nonverbal illustration, icon, product view, or abstract unlabeled visualization; otherwise remove it. 13. A real product dashboard, report, device, or application screen may appear only as the evidence-backed hero subject in the visual zone, never as a container for overlay copy.

FINAL OUTPUT: One continuous full-bleed, reference-faithful square background with a deliberately empty overlay region and one clearly art-directed visual systemÔÇöno rendered marketing copy and no logo.

Technical production contract: Renderer mapping: the left 50% is the text-safe zone and the right 50% is the visual zone; this mapping overrides any conflicting directional language above. Create negative space through subject placement, crop, lighting, blur, or a continuous color field: no text-holder box, no blank card, no placeholder panel, no empty banner, no framed copy area, and no callout rectangle. A real product screen or dashboard is allowed only as the primary evidence-backed subject in the visual zone, never as an empty copy container. No headline, no paragraph, no CTA text, no logo, no watermark, no brand name, no decorative fake text, no illegible UI labels, and no clipped primary subject.

SAFE NONVERBAL REFERENCE EVIDENCE (match these measured visual facts; never reproduce source copy or its containers): Reference 1 ÔÇö Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, White upper field transitioning through very pale blue into saturated cyan-blue across the lower third, with faint white grid lines and dotted accents over the blue-tinted area; Dominant visible colors: #FFFFFF, #F3F8FD, #0D80F4, #102F49, #111216, #4A91E8; Outer margin is approximately 7% of canvas width; foreground; Faint grid and dot field (pattern): x=0%, y=15%, width=100%, height=61%; background; Thin low-contrast white grid lines concentrated across the right and lower fields, plus small dotted matrices near the upper-right and left-middle edges.; REFERENCE BLUEPRINT: Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, White upper field transitioning through very pale blue into saturated cyan-blue across the lower third, with faint white grid lines and dotted accents over the blue-tinted area; Bright square canvas with a white upper base and blue lower transition; Right-side photography and bottom objects run into the canvas edges; Open whitespace is concentrated above the dashboard and around the upper text; Thin low-contrast white grid lines concentrated across the right and lower fields, plus small dotted matrices near the upper-right and left-middle edges; Analytics application frame (illustration): x=10%, y=40%, width=59%, height=43%; midground

OVERLAY CONTRAST CONTRACT: Keep the continuous, unboxed copy reserve close to #F3F8FD in perceived brightness and tone. The renderer will place headline text in #111216, supporting text in #111216, and accents in #0D80F4. Maintain strong readable contrast behind those colors using only a continuous field, natural light, atmosphere, crop, or blurÔÇönever a patch, card, panel, banner, or text container.

STATIC VISUAL-SIDE COMPLETENESS CONTRACT.
Every object in the visual/subject zone must be a finished, meaningful nonverbal visual. Never generate a blank or mostly blank card, white tile, empty rounded rectangle, empty dashboard widget, empty alert row, skeleton UI, placeholder panel, vacant list, blank progress bar, or module reserved for future copy anywhere on the canvas.
Filled visual modules are allowed only when each module contains a complete nonverbal illustration, icon, product view, or abstract unlabeled data visualization with no large unused interior. If a proposed module cannot be completed without generated text, delete the module and use one coherent focal subject or continuous background instead.
The only permitted empty area is the renderer copy reserve, and that reserve must be unframed negative space formed by one continuous background fieldÔÇönever a box, card, tile, row, or panel.

NONVERBAL OUTPUT CONTRACT: Return one finished square background with no readable or pseudo-readable glyphs. Preserve generous negative space for the deterministic HTML overlay. Any data visualization must be abstract, unlabeled, and decorative.', '2026-08-08T13:21:37.930603+00:00') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
