dType":"campaign-creative","observedTraits":["Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, Pale blue-white luminous background with a bright white center, cyan tint toward the side and bottom edges, faint square grid lines, large thin white concentric arcs, and a sparse white dot pattern in the upper-right corner.","Dominant visible colors: #F8FCFD, #DDF5FC, #0F2D49, #087CF0, #FFFFFF, #8ED7FF","Outer margin is approximately 7% of canvas width","AgencyAnalytics logo lockup (logo): x=36%, y=5%, width=28%, height=4%; foreground; Centered horizontal lockup with a blue circular symbol at left and the wordmark at right; Agency is thin blue text and Analytics is heavier blue text.","Primary headline (headline): x=33%, y=14%, width=34%, height=4%; foreground; Single centered line of bold dark navy text reading Reports Clients Love, with Clients highlighted in bright blue.","Supporting sentence (other): x=23%, y=21%, width=53%, height=2%; foreground; Single centered line of medium-weight dark navy text beneath the headline.","Learn More call-to-action (band): x=38%, y=28%, width=23%, height=6%; foreground; Dark navy horizontal pill with fully rounded ends and centered bold white label.","Background grid and concentric arcs (pattern): x=0%, y=24%, width=100%, height=76%; background; Very faint cyan square grid crossed by multiple oversized thin white circular arcs centered around the dashboard region; lines fade into the pale background.","Upper-right dot field (pattern): x=91%, y=1%, width=8%, height=15%; background; Sparse matrix of tiny white circular dots aligned in rows and columns, partially fading at the canvas edge.","Analytics dashboard shell (illustration): x=11%, y=40%, width=77%, height=50%; midground; Large white rounded rectangular interface panel with a thin pale border, soft gray internal shading, and broad blue-gray shadow beneath and to the right.","Dashboard navigation rail (list): x=12%, y=41%, width=7%, height=49%; foreground; Narrow white left sidebar separated by a faint vertical divider; contains one blue rounded-square selected tile followed by seven vertically spaced gray navigation icons.","Top KPI mini-card row (card): x=20%, y=43%, width=66%, height=11%; foreground; Four equal white rounded cards in one row, each with a pastel circular icon, short gray title bar, and a small colored rising line chart with a softly tinted area fill.","Large line-chart card (card): x=20%, y=56%, width=34%, height=16%; foreground; White rounded card with a short gray heading bar, faint dashed horizontal guides, one solid blue fluctuating line, one dashed blue comparison line, and pale blue area fill.","Large bar-chart card (card): x=55%, y=56%, width=31%, height=16%; foreground; White rounded card containing a short gray heading bar, faint chart axes and guides, and eight vertical blue bars of varying height.","Donut-chart card (card): x=20%, y=73%, width=31%, height=16%; foreground; White rounded card with a four-segment donut chart in blue, orange, lavender, and mint; four matching legend dots and gray label bars sit to its right.","Summary list card (card): x=53%, y=74%, width=34%, height=15%; foreground; White rounded card with a lavender circular sparkle icon, two short gray header bars, and three colored bullet rows with long pale-gray horizontal bars.","Dashboard floor shadow (other): x=11%, y=88%, width=80%, height=4%; background; Diffuse horizontal cyan-blue shadow beneath the interface, darkest near the lower corners and fading outward.","The canvas is square."],"referenceIndex":3,"allowedInfluence":["Centered logo, headline, supporting copy, and pill-button hierarchy.","Large lower-half software-report illustration anchored beneath a compact text stack.","White rounded dashboard shell with a slim left navigation rail.","Four-mini-card top row followed by two larger chart rows.","Dark navy body text paired with a single bright-blue headline highlight.","Pale cyan technical backdrop using faint grids, arcs, and restrained edge decoration.","Multicolor chart accents confined primarily to interface content.","May control the standalone-static composition, hierarchy, module anatomy, and visual treatment.","May control this ordered carousel page geometry and the repeated family system shared across the six-page sequence."],"prohibitedInferences":["Do not infer a live or functional software interface.","Do not infer any chart values, dates, labels, or business outcomes.","Do not infer people, photography, devices, or physical screens.","Do not infer a carousel sequence or neighboring pages.","Do not infer animation, hover behavior, or button destination.","Do not replace the visible analytics illustration with security, finance, or communication imagery.","Do not infer additional navigation labels from the unlabeled icons.","Do not claim the decorative arcs or grid encode data.","Do not promote a small supporting icon into the dominant hero unless its measured bounding box proves it is dominant.","Do not infer product capabilities, claims, audiences, photography, or interface behavior that is not visibly supported.","Do not enlarge a minor icon or decorative motif into the primary hero unless the measured blueprint records it as dominant."]},{"declaredType":"carousel-slide","classifiedType":"campaign-creative","observedTraits":["Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, White upper field transitioning through very pale cyan into saturated sky blue and royal blue toward the lower-right edge; faint blue grid lines, diagonal geometry, circular arcs, and small dot patterns are overlaid.","Dominant visible colors: #FFFFFF, #EAF8FF, #A9E3FF, #1687F8, #0D2942, #111111","Outer margin is approximately 3% of canvas width","AgencyAnalytics logo (logo): x=36%, y=5%, width=27%, height=4%; foreground; Centered horizontal black logo with a circular angular AA symbol at left and the wordmark at right; the Agency portion is lighter weight and Analytics is bold.","Reports Clients Love headline (headline): x=33%, y=14%, width=35%, height=4%; foreground; Centered single-line heavy sans-serif headline; Reports and Love are black while Clients is bright blue.","Supporting sentence (other): x=23%, y=21%, width=53%, height=2%; foreground; Centered single-line black bold sans-serif text reading a short statement about professional reports, time, and trust.","Learn More button (other): x=39%, y=28%, width=21%, height=6%; foreground; Dark navy horizontal pill with fully rounded ends and centered white bold label.","Faint geometric grid field (pattern): x=0%, y=3%, width=100%, height=95%; background; Very low-contrast pale-blue square grid with broad spacing, diagonal line segments, and partial geometric intersections; strongest across the left side and lower-right field.","Large circular arc (pattern): x=30%, y=24%, width=69%, height=66%; background; Thin white partial circle curving behind the laptop, with a second faint outer arc near the right edge.","Clock report card (card): x=9%, y=45%, width=19%, height=8%; midground; White rounded rectangle with soft blue-gray shadow; blue outlined clock and motion-line icon at left and two short gray text bars at right.","Sparkle report card (card): x=5%, y=54%, width=20%, height=8%; midground; White rounded rectangle with soft shadow; pale outlined circle containing two blue sparkle shapes at left and two gray text bars at right.","Document chart card (card): x=3%, y=64%, width=20%, height=8%; midground; White rounded rectangle with soft shadow; blue outlined document icon containing three ascending bars at left and two gray text bars at right.","Users report card (card): x=7%, y=73%, width=20%, height=8%; midground; White rounded rectangle with soft shadow; solid blue three-person icon at left and two gray text bars at right.","Open laptop (illustration): x=5%, y=37%, width=88%, height=56%; foreground; Large photorealistic open laptop angled in perspective, with black display bezel, dark keyboard, silver aluminum base, right-side ports, bright edge highlights, and a soft dark-blue cast shadow beneath.","Analytics dashboard on laptop screen (other): x=35%, y=40%, width=56%, height=42%; foreground; White dashboard interface clipped inside the tilted screen; black left navigation rail, blue selected navigation item, blue top accent, line chart, donut chart, world map, vertical bar chart, four compact metric tiles, and a right column of integration rows.","Lower-left dot matrix (pattern): x=1%, y=90%, width=19%, height=8%; background; Regular rows of small pale cyan and white dots fading into the blue lower-left background.","The canvas is exactly square.","The upper quarter is predominantly white."],"referenceIndex":4,"allowedInfluence":["Use a centered brand, headline, support line, and call-to-action stack in the upper third.","Use one oversized product-object illustration to dominate the lower half.","Use a staggered column of four compact feature cards beside the dominant object.","Use selective blue emphasis on one word within an otherwise black headline.","Use a white-to-blue vertical background transition with faint technical linework.","Use rounded white cards with blue icons, gray microcopy bars, and soft shadows.","Use thin circular arcs behind the dominant object as low-contrast framing.","May control the standalone-static composition, hierarchy, module anatomy, and visual treatment.","May control this ordered carousel page geometry and the repeated family system shared across the six-page sequence."],"prohibitedInferences":["Do not infer that the displayed dashboard is a functional interface.","Do not infer exact chart values, labels, dates, or performance outcomes.","Do not infer additional carousel pages or recurring sequence behavior.","Do not infer animation, hover states, or button interaction.","Do not infer people or photography beyond the visible laptop product rendering.","Do not infer security symbols, locks, shields, or circuitry.","Do not infer device models or hardware specifications.","Do not infer the full wording of small dashboard rows or card placeholders.","Do not substitute the laptop with a phone, tablet, or freestanding browser window.","Do not promote a small supporting icon into the dominant hero unless its measured bounding box proves it is dominant.","Do not infer product capabilities, claims, audiences, photography, or interface behavior that is not visibly supported."]},{"declaredType":"carousel-slide","classifiedType":"campaign-creative","observedTraits":["Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, Flat pale pink canvas with a subtle brighter pink glow behind the lower report mockup; rounded outer corners expose tiny black corner areas.","Dominant visible colors: #F9DFF5, #111116, #FFFFFF, #E699DF, #17334A, #0780ED","Outer margin is approximately 8% of canvas width","AgencyAnalytics brand mark and wordmark (logo): x=30%, y=7%, width=37%, height=6%; foreground; Centered black logo lockup comprising a circular stylized A-and-arrow symbol followed by the text AgencyAnalytics; Agency is thin and Analytics is bold.","Primary headline first line (headline): x=16%, y=17%, width=69%, height=4%; foreground; Large bold black centered text reading Simplify Client Reporting Across.","Primary headline highlighted second line (headline): x=33%, y=21%, width=31%, height=6%; foreground; Bold white text reading Every Channel inside a black rectangular highlight with slightly rounded corners.","Supporting sentence (other): x=26%, y=31%, width=48%, height=2%; foreground; Single centered line of medium-weight black text repeating the client-reporting statement.","Call-to-action button (other): x=34%, y=36%, width=29%, height=8%; foreground; Wide lavender-pink pill with fully rounded ends and centered bold black text reading See How It Works.","Report dashboard frame (card): x=12%, y=53%, width=72%, height=47%; midground; Large white-to-light-gray report interface with a faint pink shadow; its lower portion is cropped by the canvas edge.","Report title and date header (band): x=27%, y=54%, width=57%, height=6%; foreground; Pale header area with centered dark navy Campaign Performance Report title and a compact right-aligned Marketing Report label plus date range.","Google Ads logo tile (logo): x=8%, y=48%, width=18%, height=17%; foreground; White rounded square card with soft shadow, overlapping the report at upper left; contains the blue, yellow, and green Google Ads symbol.","Line-chart panel (card): x=13%, y=61%, width=35%, height=18%; foreground; White bordered chart card with a bright blue time-series line, faint horizontal grid lines, month labels, y-axis values, and a small total at upper right.","Sessions donut-chart panel (card): x=49%, y=61%, width=35%, height=18%; foreground; White bordered card containing a multicolor donut chart labeled 4,414 Sessions and a right-side legend with eight colored channel entries and values.","KPI card row (KPI): x=13%, y=81%, width=71%, height=8%; foreground; Six adjacent white outlined metric cards showing Sessions, Avg. Session Duration, New Sessions, Bounce Rate, Goal Completions, and Pages/Session with large dark navy values.","Tabular report section (list): x=13%, y=90%, width=71%, height=10%; foreground; White data-table area cropped at the bottom, with a row-count note, five visible column headings, divider rules, and the beginning of a Direct data row.","Orange platform logo tile (logo): x=73%, y=86%, width=19%, height=14%; foreground; Large white rounded square card with soft shadow, cropped by the bottom edge; an angular orange glyph is centered inside and partially visible.","The canvas is exactly square.","The outer canvas has rounded corners."],"referenceIndex":5,"allowedInfluence":["Centered brand, headline, supporting copy, and CTA hierarchy","Black rectangular emphasis behind one headline line","Large lower-half report or document mockup","Overlapping square integration-logo tiles at opposing report corners","Pink, black, white, and dark-navy color relationships","A chart row followed by a compact KPI row and table","Intentional bottom-edge crop of the dominant report object","May control the standalone-static composition, hierarchy, module anatomy, and visual treatment.","May control this ordered carousel page geometry and the repeated family system shared across the six-page sequence."],"prohibitedInferences":["Do not infer a multi-page carousel or repeated slide sequence.","Do not infer any people, photography, devices, or physical environment.","Do not infer charts or metrics beyond those visibly shown.","Do not interpret the white report as a laptop or browser window.","Do not infer additional integration logos outside the two visible tiles.","Do not infer animation, hover behavior, or CTA interaction.","Do not infer a background gradient; only a localized lower glow is visible.","Do not infer unseen content below the cropped canvas edge.","Do not promote a small supporting icon into the dominant hero unless its measured bounding box proves it is dominant.","Do not infer product capabilities, claims, audiences, photography, or interface behavior that is not visibly supported.","Do not enlarge a minor icon or decorative motif into the primary hero unless the measured blueprint records it as dominant."]},{"declaredType":"carousel-slide","classifiedType":"campaign-creative","observedTraits":["Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, Flat pale peach canvas with a faint warmer peach glow behind the lower dashboard-card cluster; rounded outer canvas corners.","Dominant visible colors: #FFE9CF, #111219, #FFFFFF, #FBBE73, #0879E8, #B3DE3D","Outer margin is approximately 7% of canvas width","AgencyAnalytics brand lockup (logo): x=30%, y=7%, width=37%, height=6%; foreground; Centered black brand mark followed by the AgencyAnalytics wordmark; the first word uses a thin weight and Analytics uses a heavy weight.","Primary headline first line (headline): x=16%, y=17%, width=65%, height=4%; foreground; Large bold black centered text reading Simplify Client Reporting Across.","Black headline highlight band (band): x=33%, y=21%, width=31%, height=6%; midground; Solid near-black horizontal rectangle with slightly rounded corners.","Highlighted headline second line (headline): x=34%, y=22%, width=29%, height=4%; foreground; Large bold white centered text reading Every Channel, contained within the black band.","Supporting sentence (other): x=26%, y=31%, width=44%, height=2%; foreground; Single line of medium-size black centered text repeating the reporting statement.","Call-to-action button (band): x=34%, y=36%, width=29%, height=8%; foreground; Wide orange-peach pill with fully rounded ends and centered bold near-black text reading See How It Works.","Sessions donut dashboard card (card): x=7%, y=48%, width=57%, height=31%; foreground; Large white rounded card with a thin light-gray inner frame and soft warm shadow; contains a Sessions label, multicolor donut chart, central 4,414 Sessions KPI, and an eight-row colored legend with values.","Multicolor sessions donut (illustration): x=16%, y=55%, width=19%, height=19%; foreground; Ring chart divided into eight colored segments in lime, yellow, pink, beige, light blue, orange, cyan, and muted blue; white center contains dark KPI text.","Sessions line-chart card (card): x=66%, y=53%, width=26%, height=14%; foreground; White rounded card with pale border and warm shadow; a blue time-series line sits over faint horizontal gridlines, with Sessions at upper left and 41,965 at upper right.","Goal Completions KPI module (KPI): x=67%, y=69%, width=12%, height=9%; foreground; White rectangular KPI tile with thin gray border, small Goal Completions label, and large centered dark value 778.","Pages per Session KPI module (KPI): x=80%, y=69%, width=12%, height=9%; foreground; White rectangular KPI tile with thin gray border, small Pages/Session label, and large centered dark value 5.27.","Channel data table card (card): x=20%, y=80%, width=72%, height=20%; foreground; Wide white rounded card with a thin light-gray inner frame and soft warm shadow; cropped by the bottom canvas edge. It contains a row-count note, six column headers, horizontal dividers, and multiple channel-data rows.","The canvas is square.","The base field is pale peach.","All primary copy is horizontally centered."],"referenceIndex":6,"allowedInfluence":["Centered single-page hero composition with brand, headline, support line, and CTA stacked vertically.","Selective black reverse-text highlight applied to one headline line.","Asymmetric dashboard collage using one large left card and smaller right modules.","White analytics cards with restrained borders and soft shadows over a pale peach field.","Bottom-edge cropping of a wide table to imply additional content below the canvas.","Use of a multicolor donut, blue line chart, and paired KPI tiles in the measured positions.","May control the standalone-static composition, hierarchy, module anatomy, and visual treatment.","May control this ordered carousel page geometry and the repeated family system shared across the six-page sequence."],"prohibitedInferences":["Do not infer people, photography, devices, or environmental scenes.","Do not infer a navigation bar or menu links.","Do not infer additional carousel pages or repeated slide rules.","Do not infer animation or interactivity from the static charts and button.","Do not infer dashboard controls beyond the visible labels and table indicator.","Do not replace the donut chart with a pie chart, gauge, or unrelated illustration.","Do not add icons to the CTA.","Do not infer a full-page gradient; only a faint warm glow is visible near the card cluster.","Do not infer uncropped table rows below the canvas.","Do not infer additional KPI cards beyond the two visible modules.","Do not promote a small supporting icon into the dominant hero unless its measured bounding box proves it is dominant."]},{"declaredType":"carousel-slide","classifiedType":"campaign-creative","observedTraits":["Canvas: landscape, aspect 1.2:1, Flat white canvas with large pastel geometric shapes entering from the lower edge and right edge; a pale pink triangular field rises from the bottom-left, a lavender-to-pink semicircular mound sits behind the report interface, and a saturated purple diagonal wedge occupies the right side.","Dominant visible colors: #FFFFFF, #0875F5, #102D47, #A974E8, #D2A0D8, #F0C3BC","Outer margin is approximately 7% of canvas width","AgencyAnalytics brand mark (logo): x=36%, y=9%, width=28%, height=5%; foreground; Centered blue circular A symbol with a small white chart-sheet motif, followed by the blue AgencyAnalytics wordmark; the final word segment is heavier.","Two-line reporting headline (headline): x=28%, y=20%, width=47%, height=13%; foreground; Large bold centered sans-serif text on two lines; the opening words ''One Platform'' are bright blue while the remaining words are dark navy.","View Features button (other): x=37%, y=40%, width=26%, height=9%; foreground; Dark navy horizontal pill with fully rounded ends and centered bold white label.","Right purple diagonal field (band): x=87%, y=39%, width=13%, height=61%; background; Large purple field entering from the right edge with a long diagonal upper-left boundary; lower area shifts toward pink-purple.","Central pastel semicircular mound (other): x=23%, y=55%, width=41%, height=22%; background; Wide upper half-circle behind the product interface, transitioning from pale pink-lavender at left to stronger violet at right; lower portion is obscured.","Bottom-left pink geometric field (other): x=0%, y=80%, width=25%, height=20%; background; Pale blush polygon rising diagonally from the lower-left edge with a warmer muted rose overlay near its upper-right portion.","Amazon integration tile (card): x=0%, y=56%, width=10%, height=12%; foreground; White rounded square cropped by the left edge, carrying a gray lowercase Amazon a and pale orange smile-arrow; faint warm shadow.","LinkedIn integration tile (card): x=18%, y=47%, width=10%, height=12%; foreground; White rounded square with a light-blue rounded LinkedIn icon and white ''in'' lettering; soft peach-gray shadow.","Google Analytics integration tile (card): x=49%, y=59%, width=10%, height=12%; foreground; White rounded square containing three orange/yellow analytics bars and dots; pronounced warm shadow cast down-right.","Shopify integration tile (card): x=76%, y=64%, width=10%, height=12%; foreground; White rounded square with a green Shopify shopping-bag symbol; warm shadow beneath and to the right.","Google Ads integration tile (card): x=5%, y=71%, width=10%, height=15%; foreground; White rounded square over the interface, containing the multicolor Google Ads angled mark; soft peach shadow.","Facebook integration tile (card): x=87%, y=86%, width=10%, height=12%; foreground; White rounded square containing a blue circle and white lowercase Facebook f; cropped close to the right edge with warm shadow.","Digital marketing report interface (illustration): x=12%, y=65%, width=81%, height=35%; midground; Large cropped software/report screen extending through the bottom edge. It has a white top title row, thin gray dividers, blue active tabs, a left navigation list, a central report page with date and line-chart content, and a right widget panel.","Google Business Profile integration tile (card): x=30%, y=90%, width=10%, height=10%; foreground; Partially cropped white rounded square at the bottom, holding a blue storefront awning and white G symbol; warm shadow visible around its upper and right edges.","Partially visible purple integration tile (card): x=9%, y=96%, width=10%, height=4%; foreground; Only the rounded white card top and upper arc of a purple circular symbol are visible at the bottom edge."],"referenceIndex":7,"allowedInfluence":["Centered brand-to-headline-to-button hierarchy on a white field.","Lower-third product screenshot composition with edge cropping.","Floating rounded integration-logo cards surrounding a software interface.","Blue and navy text hierarchy paired with pastel lavender and blush geometry.","Warm card shadows used to separate white tiles from a white background.","Asymmetric edge-entering geometric fields behind the product view.","May control the standalone-static composition, hierarchy, module anatomy, and visual treatment.","May control this ordered carousel page geometry and the repeated family system shared across the six-page sequence."],"prohibitedInferences":["Do not infer animation, carousel behavior, or interaction states.","Do not infer additional pages or recurring sequence rules.","Do not invent people, devices, photographs, or environmental scenes.","Do not interpret the screenshot as a live or functional dashboard.","Do not infer integrations beyond the logos visibly shown.","Do not add security symbols, shields, locks, circuits, or abstract technology motifs.","Do not replace the geometric backdrop with a full-canvas gradient.","Do not assume hidden content below the cropped canvas.","Do not promote a small supporting icon into the dominant hero unless its measured bounding box proves it is dominant.","Do not infer product capabilities, claims, audiences, photography, or interface behavior that is not visibly supported.","Do not enlarge a minor icon or decorative motif into the primary hero unless the measured blueprint records it as dominant."]}],"uncertainties":["Cross-slide family rules are compiled from independent page measurements; confirm any rule that is not visibly repeated across the ordered source pages."],"sourcePriority":["brand-guideline document","reference images","website"],"repeatedPatterns":["A small blue eyebrow is positioned above the main title.","Black, white, and bright blue form the visible identity contrast.","Rounded white interface panels use subtle shadows.","The bottom-left black pill serves as the visible brand anchor.","The copy and identity badge share the same approximate left margin.","Maintain the square canvas and approximately 5.5% outer text margin.","Keep the complete copy block in the upper-left quadrant.","Keep the headline on one line with only its latter phrase inside a black rounded block.","Preserve exactly two bullet rows beneath the supporting statement.","Keep the large desktop panel as the dominant lower-half object.","Retain the phone-left, dashboard-center, calendar-right overlap sequence.","Keep the black identity pill overlapping the phone near the bottom-left.","Centered black handle capsule as a visible identity anchor.","Centered typographic axis shared by headline, support line, and CTA.","Edge-cropped blue-and-white data graphics as peripheral framing.","Bright upper whitespace transitioning into a denser blue lower field.","Preserve substantial open space above the calendar and to the right of the headline.","Keep the square canvas and full-bleed white-to-blue vertical transition.","Keep the identity capsule centered near the top.","Keep the headline and supporting statement centered on the same vertical axis."]},"brandDescription":"## Brand summary\nAgencyAnalytics is an AI-powered marketing analytics and client-reporting platform purpose-built for marketing agencies. It brings client data from more than 85 sources into one place, then helps agency teams analyze performance, surface meaningful trends, and deliver polished reports and dashboards without spreadsheet-heavy or conventional BI workflows. The audience includes agency owners, account managers, strategists, analysts, client-service teams, and the clients who consume their reporting.\n\nThe central problem is reporting chaos: fragmented channel data, repetitive manual production, unclear performance narratives, and too little time for strategy. AgencyAnalytics addresses that problem with automated reports, customizable dashboards, reusable templates, drag-and-drop editing, AI-assisted analysis, alerts, anomaly detection, forecasting, benchmarks, client portals, white labeling, task management, and access controls. Its strongest differentiation is the combination of agency-specific workflows, multi-client visibility, client-ready presentation, broad data connectivity, and analysis that turns raw metrics into useful next steps.\n\nThe brand should consistently connect operational efficiency to a client outcome: agencies save time, explain results clearly, prove ROI, and make reporting a reason clients stay. Verified proof includes use by 7,000+ marketing agencies, 85+ data sources or integrations, and a reported 4.7/5 rating across G2 and Capterra based on 500+ reviews. The self-service offer includes a free 14-day trial with no credit card required.\n\nDerived direction: Carry forward the idea of AgencyAnalytics as the agency-specific operating layer that turns scattered client data into clear, branded client intelligence at scale. Every campaign should make the path from data to insight to client confidence easy to understand.\n\n## Visual identity\nThe verified asset set includes an AgencyAnalytics combination logo and large and small wordmark assets. The recognizable horizontal lockup combines an angular symbol with the single-line AgencyAnalytics wordmark; observed executions distinguish the two parts of the name through weight, with Agency lighter and Analytics heavier. Official and campaign examples use both blue and black presentations, so production teams should select an existing supplied asset rather than reconstructing the mark or approximating the wordmark.\n\nThe visual system is recognizable through a concentrated set of cues:\n\n- Bright blue paired with dark navy or near-black, white, and pale blue surfaces.\n- Clean, rounded interface cards with restrained shadows and visible data visualizations.\n- Product panels arranged as modular layers rather than hidden inside decorative scenery.\n- Upward movement expressed through the angular mark, charts, progress lines, goals, and performance indicators.\n- Pale grids, dotted accents, circular outlines, arcs, diagonal geometry, and blue-tinted lower fields in campaign compositions.\n- A clear split between concise campaign copy and a substantial product proof area.\n\nDerived direction: The visual personality should feel capable, clear, optimistic, and operationally calm. Make complex data look manageable without making the brand simplistic. For square campaign work, anchor the logo and copy in the upper portion and let a large product panel or layered UI cluster dominate the lower half. Use abstraction to frame the information, not to compete with it.\n\nNo verified clear-space ratio, minimum logo size, alternate-mark taxonomy, or corporate-logo background specification is supplied. Do not create numerical logo rules from preview guides or apply customer white-label upload requirements to the AgencyAnalytics corporate identity.\n\n## Color palette\nNo authoritative guideline color table was supplied. The following exact values come from measured campaign references and should be treated as the working digital palette for matching those executions, not as print or Pantone specifications:\n\n- **#0D80F4 ÔÇö primary bright blue:** Brand emphasis, highlighted words, active interface states, links, primary controls, and dominant chart lines.\n- **#102F49 ÔÇö dark navy:** Headings, high-emphasis supporting copy, dark buttons, and strong UI labels where a softer alternative to black is useful.\n- **#4A91E8 ÔÇö supporting blue:** Secondary chart emphasis, lighter interface accents, and tonal depth within blue compositions.\n- **#111216 ÔÇö near-black:** Primary text, black logo treatments, dark highlight bands, and maximum-emphasis campaign elements.\n- **#F3F8FD ÔÇö pale blue:** Section fields, soft transitions, low-emphasis panels, and spacious background areas.\n- **#FFFFFF ÔÇö white:** Main content surfaces, interface cards, reversed copy, and open negative space.\n\nObserved product visualizations add categorical colors such as cyan, green, lime, yellow, orange, pink, red, teal, lavender, and muted tan. These colors distinguish channels, segments, ranking bands, or status; they do not replace bright blue as the main brand and interaction color. Green is repeatedly associated with positive movement or enabled settings, while red can indicate negative or lower-status conditions. Client-specific white-label palettes are demonstrations of product flexibility and must not be mistaken for the AgencyAnalytics corporate palette.\n\nDerived direction: Build hierarchy with white or pale blue as the field, near-black or navy for primary reading, and #0D80F4 for the single most important phrase, control, or data signal. Keep secondary chart colors functionally distinct and restrained. No formal accessibility pairings were supplied, so validate contrast in the final medium rather than assuming that an observed pairing is compliant; use high-contrast navy or near-black for essential text and reserve light blue-on-white combinations for nonessential decoration.\n\n## Typography\nNo authoritative corporate typeface or licensed font family is identified in the supplied guideline material. Measured campaign references use an `Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif` implementation stack, with approximately 700 weight for headings and 400 for body copy. Treat this as a reproducible reference for the supplied creative, not as confirmation of a proprietary brand font.\n\nObserved hierarchy is consistent even where the exact family is unavailable:\n\n- Large headlines use a bold sans serif, short line lengths, and direct outcome-led phrasing.\n- Body copy uses a regular, highly legible sans serif with enough spacing to keep operational language approachable.\n- Product titles and field labels use clear weight changes rather than decorative styling.\n- KPI numerals are large and bold; descriptors, legends, and table labels are smaller and quieter.\n- Small uppercase eyebrow labels may introduce a category or workflow, while primary headlines and body copy remain sentence case.\n- Campaign emphasis may color one key word bright blue or place the latter phrase in a dark rounded block with white type.\n\nDerived direction: Typography should sound like an experienced agency operator: decisive in the headline, plainspoken in the explanation, and precise in the data. Use weight, color, and compact phrase grouping to establish hierarchy. Avoid expressive display lettering, excessive all-caps copy, or dense paragraphs that make the platform feel more complicated than the workflow it replaces.\n\n## Style\nThe official messaging pattern is direct, practical, second-person, and agency-literate. It names a familiar operational problem, explains the workflow, and closes on a business outcome. Recurring concepts include `client-ready`, `prove ROI`, `save time`, `one place`, `without the manual work`, `white label`, `insights`, `client intelligence`, and `reporting chaos`. Prefer concrete verbs such as connect, automate, track, surface, share, monitor, compare, customize, and scale. Explain results in plain English rather than adding BI jargon.\n\n## CTA\nThe primary self-service CTA language is `Start Free`, `Start Free Trial`, or, in the closing conversion section, `Start Your Free Trial Today`. Pair trial conversion with the verified reassurance `Free 14-day trial. No credit card required.` The assisted-sales alternative is `Book Demo` or `Book a Demo`.\n\nThe recurring action hierarchy is:\n\n- **Primary conversion:** `Start Free` or `Start Free Trial` for users ready to enter the product.\n- **Secondary conversion:** `Book Demo` or `Book a Demo` for buyers who want a guided, agency-specific walkthrough.\n- **Product education:** `Watch the Platform Tour`.\n- **Workflow discovery:** `Start With a Template` and `Find Your Integrations`.\n- **Solution progression:** `Speed Up Client Onboarding`, `Strengthen Client Relationships`, and `Maintain Complete Client Visibility`.\n\nPrimary and secondary conversion actions appear together immediately after high-level value propositions; trial language is also repeated near the end of the page. Supporting CTAs sit beside the workflow or resource they describe. Action language is concise, imperative, and specific rather than abstract.\n\nDerived direction: Preserve the two-track conversion model in campaign work: immediate product access first, human guidance second. Use one primary CTA and at most one assisted alternative in a single static unit. Do not invent discounts, guarantees, urgency, or trial terms beyond the verified 14-day and no-credit-card statements.\n\n## Background imagery\nEvidenced imagery includes bright workplace photography, attributed customer headshots, team collaboration, and product-focused compositions. People are shown discussing work, using laptops, or participating in agency activity rather than posing as generic technology users. Lighting is natural and bright, environments are warm and neutral, and the overall treatment remains realistic and full color.\n\nProduct-led backgrounds use white or pale blue fields transitioning into more saturated cyan or royal blue, often in the lower third. Repeated decorative ingredients include faint square grids, sparse dots, oversized circular outlines, thin arcs, diagonal shapes, and soft tonal glows. Other campaign references use flat pale pink or peach fields behind report and dashboard mockups. A saturated blue report-cover treatment with an oversized cropped angular or swooping form is also evidenced.\n\nDerived direction: Choose a background according to the proof being shown. Use a clean pale field for dense UI, a blue gradient field for broad platform or intelligence messaging, and workplace photography when the idea depends on agency collaboration or time returned to people. Preserve an uncluttered area for the headline and CTA. Crop photography so faces and working gestures remain clear while the less active side of the frame accepts UI overlays.\n\nDerived direction: Avoid busy stock-office scenes, dark cinematic technology imagery, heavy textures, fake data tunnels, or scenic lifestyle backgrounds with no relationship to agency work. Do not place essential copy over the most detailed part of a photograph or dashboard.\n\n## UI mockup\nFor the central campaign messageÔÇöturning client data into client intelligenceÔÇöthe most relevant verified workflow is a unified client dashboard paired with AI analysis that surfaces trends, dips, opportunities, summaries, or recommended next steps. This shows both halves of the promise: connected performance data and the interpretation that makes it actionable. If a campaign instead focuses on automation, use report scheduling; for branding, use a white-labeled dashboard or report; for proactive monitoring, use anomaly annotations or metric alerts; for retention, use the client portal; and for operational visibility, use a multi-client dashboard, roll-up view, goals, or tasks.\n\nObserved marketing treatments show the interface directly as a front-facing application window or cropped panel rather than inside a laptop or phone frame. Screens may include real reports, dashboards, KPI cards, charts, tables, the drag-and-drop builder, AI Summary, Ask AI, scheduling controls, client overview, goals, anomaly detection, access management, or task management. Use only approved product captures and existing interface states; do not fabricate navigation, client names, metrics, trends, alerts, AI answers, or integrations.\n\nDerived direction: For the default intelligence campaign, place one large front-facing dashboard in the lower or right portion of the composition and pull one verified AI insight or analysis panel forward as the focal interaction. Keep perspective minimal so labels and visualizations remain credible. Show a small number of KPI cards and one principal chart or table rather than an unreadable wall of widgets. Leave the upper-left or opposite side clear for headline, support copy, and CTA; no essential text should overlap the UI.\n\nDerived direction: Device framing is unnecessary unless an approved source asset already uses it or mobile access is itself the message. Human-plus-product scenes are appropriate when the campaign is about collaboration, client conversations, or time saved; otherwise, direct product evidence is stronger. When no verified screen directly supports the claim, use no UI rather than inventing one.\n\n## Icons and illustration\nThe evidenced icon role is functional and informational. Product controls use compact symbols for reports, dashboards, charts, alerts, integrations, users, time, close, add, dropdown, and AI or sparkle actions. They are generally simple, low-detail, and monochrome in dark navy or gray, with blue used for active, selected, or branded actions. An extracted analytics integration asset uses three colored bars, while third-party integration logos retain their recognizable forms and original colors.\n\nStandalone illustration is not the dominant system. Marketing work relies more on direct product screenshots, photography-plus-UI collage, charts, geometric fields, and the angular directional geometry associated with the brand mark. Circular avatars, initials, and profile photos may support collaboration or access-management scenes.\n\nDerived direction: Use icons to clarify controls, categories, or stepsÔÇönot as the main visual spectacle. Keep forms compact and geometric, maintain consistent apparent stroke weight within a single set, and avoid mixing detailed pictograms with minimal interface symbols. Preserve original integration logos when naming real connected platforms rather than redrawing them into a house style.\n\nDerived direction: If illustration is required, keep it geometric, data-oriented, and subordinate to product evidence. Suitable ingredients are charts, progress paths, modular cards, directional arrows, grids, and cropped angular forms. Do not introduce mascots, hand-drawn editorial characters, elaborate isometric worlds, or unrelated 3D iconography; no such system is evidenced.","visualBlueprints":{"staticSystem":{"zones":["AgencyAnalytics logo lockup (logo): x=7%, y=5%, width=26%, height=4%; foreground; Black circular angular emblem followed by the black wordmark; the second word is heavier than the first","Reports Clients Love headline (headline): x=8%, y=14%, width=34%, height=4%; foreground; Single-line bold sans-serif headline in black, with the middle word Clients highlighted in bright blue","Supporting statement (other): x=8%, y=21%, width=50%, height=6%; foreground; Two lines of heavy black sans-serif text, left aligned, with a wide line break after the words save time","Learn More button (other): x=7%, y=34%, width=20%, height=6%; foreground; Dark navy horizontal pill with centered bold white label","Faint grid and dot field (pattern): x=0%, y=15%, width=100%, height=61%; background; Thin low-contrast white grid lines concentrated across the right and lower fields, plus small dotted matrices near the upper-right and left-middle edges","Analytics application frame (illustration): x=10%, y=40%, width=59%, height=43%; midground; Large white rounded software window with a dark vertical navigation rail, pale top toolbar, light gray card borders, and soft shadow; its lower-right area is obscured","Main line-chart card (card): x=16%, y=47%, width=29%, height=11%; midground; Wide white rounded card with pale horizontal guides, gray label strokes, and a thin blue rising line graph","Donut-chart card (KPI): x=46%, y=47%, width=20%, height=11%; midground; White rounded card containing a blue and pale-gray donut chart, four blue circular legend marks, and gray text strokes","Three compact chart cards (card): x=16%, y=59%, width=50%, height=9%; midground; Row of three white rounded modules: a blue line chart, an orange line chart, and a seven-column blue bar chart","Lower dashboard modules (card): x=16%, y=70%, width=50%, height=1