shared by headline, support line, and CTA.","Edge-cropped blue-and-white data graphics as peripheral framing.","Bright upper whitespace transitioning into a denser blue lower field.","Preserve substantial open space above the calendar and to the right of the headline.","Keep the square canvas and full-bleed white-to-blue vertical transition.","Keep the identity capsule centered near the top.","Keep the headline and supporting statement centered on the same vertical axis."]},"carouselLayouts":[{"name":"Demo Brand Reference-Faithful Sequence","slides":[{"role":"title","prompt":"PURPOSE: Build the title page of the reference-faithful Demo Brand carousel as a square 1:1, 1080x1080 full-bleed background. Deterministic HTML overlays add every real word, logo, and CTA.\n\nEVIDENCE BASIS: Reference 2 ÔÇö Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, White upper field transitioning through very pale blue at mid-height into saturated cyan and royal blue across the lower third; faint blue grid lines, dots, and oversized circular outlines are overlaid on the right and lower areas.; Dominant visible colors: #FFFFFF, #F1F8FF, #0878EF, #079BF2, #102F4B, #111216; Outer margin is approximately 7% of canvas width; AgencyAnalytics deterministic overlay reserve lockup (deterministic overlay reserve): x=7%, y=5%, width=27%, height=4%; foreground; Black circular emblem containing an angular white-and-black mark, followed by the black wordmark; the second word is visibly heavier than the first.; Primary headline (headline): x=8%, y=14%, width=34%, height=4%; foreground; Single-line bold sans-serif headline reading ''Reports Clients Love''; black text with only ''Clients'' colored bright blue.; Supporting statement (headline): x=8%, y=21%, width=49%, height=6%; foreground; Two lines of heavy black sans-serif text, left aligned, with a generous line gap and a period at the end.; Learn More button (other): x=7%, y=33%, width=20%, height=6%; foreground; Dark navy horizontal pill with fully rounded ends and centered bold white label.; Analytics dashboard panel (card): x=5%, y=43%, width=53%, height=35%; midground; Large translucent white rounded rectangle with a faint blue-gray border and soft shadow. A narrow left navigation rail contains six small blue-gray icons and one selected blue home tile. The main area contains four white data cards: line chart, donut with legend, vertical bars, and two-line trend chart..\n\nREFERENCE BLUEPRINT: Preserve this page-specific measured composition. SHARED FAMILY EVIDENCE: Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, Full-bleed pale cyan field with a soft white glow through the center and slightly stronger cyan tint toward the outer edges and lower corners.; Dominant visible colors: #DDF8FF, #FFFFFF, #000000, #0786F5, #20242A, #E9EEF2; Outer margin is approximately 6% of canvas width; Square 1:1 canvas with full-bleed pale cyan coloring.; Diffuse near-white illumination occupies the center behind the text and interface panels.; Edges remain unframed and slightly more cyan than the center.; Primary left margin is approximately 5.5%; rightmost visible object ends near 94.2%.; No border, footer band, or corner decoration is visible.; Canvas: square, aspect 1:1, Full-bleed white field transitioning vertically into pale cyan through the middle and saturated sky blue at the bottom; faint white network lines, nodes, dotted patterns, and translucent interface panels overlay the lower half.; Dominant visible colors: #FFFFFF, #EAF8FF, #BDEBFF, #56B9F5, #168EEA, #111116; Bright square canvas with a white upper field and cyan-to-blue lower transition.; Full-bleed color reaches all four edges with no enclosing border.\n\nCOPY ANALYSIS: Analyze the supplied title copy for message length, whether it contains a statistic, comparison, list, process, or action, and its strongest proof. Adapt the content density to this page; never invent an extra message merely to occupy a reference module.\n\nSCENE SELECTION: product or software copy ÔåÆ use one evidence-backed device, dashboard, report, or UI as the hero subject; people or service copy ÔåÆ use one evidence-backed person, workplace, vehicle, or environmental subject; statistic or proof ÔåÆ use one unlabeled abstract motif only if the reference supports it; risk or problem ÔåÆ use one tension object; action or process ÔåÆ use one practical subject; short title ÔåÆ use one small visual cluster and generous negative space; no clear match ÔåÆ preserve page geometry and reduce detail.\n\nROLE-SPECIFIC ANATOMY: Cover: use one restrained evidence-backed hero subject in the visual zone and leave the fixed headline area open.\n\nLAYOUT: Keep the left 62% as continuous quiet negative space and the right 38% as the visual zone. The primary visual must remain on the right; deterministic text renders on the left. Puppeteer owns the overlay coordinates: text (0, 120), logo (60, 48), CTA (60, 900). The background must not draw a boundary, panel, card, banner, box, or placeholder around those coordinates. Preserve the measured crop, outer margin, and subject scale. Generated subjects and subtle patterns stay in the complementary visual zone. Do not generate navigation arrows, text bands, cards, or panels; the application adds functional overlays later.\n\nVISUAL EXECUTION: Retain the evidence-backed canvas brightness, palette placement, continuous background construction, illustration or photographic medium, shadow language, and recurring family rhythm. Evidence-backed product UI may remain inside the hero subject; never reproduce a band, card, or panel as a holder for renderer copy. The title page must remain recognizably related to the other five pages while its subject hierarchy stays unique.\n\nDENSITY: Use one focal subject grouping plus at most two small evidence-backed supporting objects. Maintain a clear foreground, restrained midground, quiet continuous background, and immediate three-second comprehension.\n\nRESTRICTIONS: 1. Do not promote a minor reference icon into the primary hero. 2. Do not invent claims, metrics, people, photography, UI, or product capabilities. 3. Do not replace the measured family background with generic neon cybersecurity art. 4. Do not move generated visuals into the deterministic text-safe zone. 5. Do not render headline, paragraph, CTA, logo, watermark, brand name, or decorative fake text. 6. Do not change the observed illustration medium, depth, subject construction, or palette placement. Preserve real product UI only when it is the evidence-backed hero subject. 7. Do not reuse the same visual scene on another role; each page keeps its own measured anatomy. 8. Do not break the shared outer margin, navigation anchor, or recurring family rhythm. 9. Do not draw blank cards, empty panels, placeholder rectangles, statistic boxes, text-holder banners, fake forms, or framed copy areas. 10. A real evidence-backed product UI may be the hero subject in the visual zone, but it may not be simplified into an empty box for later text.\n\nFINAL OUTPUT: One continuous full-bleed carousel background with a deliberately empty renderer-aligned copy reserve, exact reference-derived page anatomy, no rendered marketing copy, and no logo.\n\nTechnical production contract: Renderer mapping: the left 62% is the text-safe zone and the right 38% is the visual zone; this mapping overrides any conflicting directional language above. Create negative space through subject placement, crop, lighting, blur, or a continuous color field: no text-holder box, no blank card, no placeholder panel, no empty banner, no framed copy area, and no callout rectangle. A real product screen or dashboard is allowed only as the primary evidence-backed subject in the visual zone, never as an empty copy container. No headline, no paragraph, no CTA text, no logo, no watermark, no brand name, no decorative fake text, no illegible UI labels, and no clipped primary subject.","slideIndex":1,"puppeteerConfig":{"cta":null,"logoX":60,"logoY":48,"textX":0,"textY":120,"bgColor":